---
source: crates/transit_agent/src/tool_schemas.rs
assertion_line: 380
expression: bundle
---
- description: "List currently-open sessions. Call this first when you need to know which devices are reachable. Takes no input. Returns each session's id, device id, vendor, transport kind, and opened-at timestamp. Session ids are short stable aliases (\"s1\", \"s2\", …) — use them verbatim in every session_id parameter. The device id is the connection name the user chose for the device (e.g. \"R1\") — when the user refers to a device by name, match it against device_id to pick the session."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties: {}
    type: object
  name: list_open_sessions
- description: "Read recent PTY output from an open session. Call this to observe what's already on the user's screen — config dumps, log lines, prompts. Output is filtered through the redaction filter before you see it (PEM keys, passwords, tokens replaced with [REDACTED:…] markers). PREFER a `match` needle over reading whole rings — it keeps only matching lines plus context and reports `total_matched`, so you spend context on the lines that answer the question. Cap plain reads with `max_bytes`."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      context_lines:
        description: Lines of context kept around each match. Defaults to 2; capped at 10.
        minimum: 0
        type: integer
      match:
        description: "Keep only lines containing this LITERAL substring (case-sensitive, not a regex), plus context_lines around each hit. The result reports total_matched so you know what you did not see."
        type: string
      max_bytes:
        description: Maximum bytes to return. Defaults to 16384.
        minimum: 1
        type: integer
      session_id:
        description: "Target session id from list_open_sessions (e.g. \"s1\")."
        type: string
    required:
      - session_id
    type: object
  name: read_scrollback
- description: "Propose a command to execute in a session. Every proposal runs through both the per-vendor policy gate AND a UI approval modal — both, never one or the other. The user can approve, deny, or approve-and-remember (a regex allowlist scoped to this chat session). On approval, the command runs and the captured output is returned (already redacted). A `capture=\"silence\"` attribute on the result envelope means the output ended on quiet with no prompt — the command may still be running; re-read the scrollback rather than inventing the missing tail. On deny / gate-block, `executed: false` plus a reason is returned so you can pivot."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      command:
        description: Single command line. Read-only verbs only — write/config commands are denied at the gate.
        type: string
      session_id:
        description: "Target session id from list_open_sessions (e.g. \"s1\")."
        type: string
    required:
      - session_id
      - command
    type: object
  name: propose_command
- description: "Ask the user a clarifying question. Use this when you genuinely need information you can't derive from scrollback — never as a substitute for proposing a command. The user's reply is returned verbatim."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      question:
        description: "Single, focused question. Multi-question prompts confuse the user."
        type: string
    required:
      - question
    type: object
  name: ask_user
- description: "Propose a read-only GET against an API/controller session (e.g. a UniFi controller shown by list_open_sessions). GET-ONLY: there is deliberately no `method` field — you cannot request a write. Like propose_command it runs the gate (GET-only + host-pin) AND a user approval modal — both, every call. `path` is relative to the controller's fixed API base (e.g. \"/v1/sites\"); the host is fixed to the controller. On approval the GET runs and the already-redacted JSON body is returned; on deny/decline `executed: false` plus a reason. Use this for API/controller sessions; use propose_command for SSH/console sessions."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      path:
        description: "Path (with optional ?query) relative to the controller's API base, e.g. /v1/sites. GET only."
        type: string
      session_id:
        description: "Target API session id from list_open_sessions (e.g. \"s2\")."
        type: string
    required:
      - session_id
      - path
    type: object
  name: propose_api_call
- description: "Query an open packet capture. START WITH `{\"kind\": \"overview\"}` — it is a precomputed digest (protocol mix, top talkers, conversations, TCP health, DNS/TLS/HTTP summaries, and deterministic findings) that costs the same whether the capture holds a thousand packets or ten million. Then drill in: `packets` for rows matching a view filter, `conversations` for the flow table, `flow` for one conversation's story, `packet` for one packet's fields, `findings` for the full problem list, `timeline` for rates over time. Findings carry a ready-made filter showing their evidence — use it. Filters use Transit's syntax: `tcp.port == 443 and ip.src == 10.0.0.0/24 and dns.rcode != 0`. This tool reads a local file and changes nothing. It returns dissected fields and summaries only; packet payload is not available through it."
  input_schema:
    additionalProperties: false
    properties:
      capture_id:
        description: Which open capture. Omit when only one is open.
        type: string
      query:
        description: "What to ask. Pick one `kind`."
        oneOf:
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              kind:
                const: list
            required:
              - kind
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              kind:
                const: overview
            required:
              - kind
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              filter:
                description: "View filter, e.g. `tcp.port == 443`."
                type: string
              kind:
                const: packets
              limit:
                maximum: 500
                minimum: 1
                type: integer
              offset:
                minimum: 0
                type: integer
            required:
              - kind
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              by:
                enum:
                  - bytes
                  - packets
                  - duration
                  - retransmits
                  - start
                type: string
              kind:
                const: conversations
              limit:
                maximum: 500
                minimum: 1
                type: integer
            required:
              - kind
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              flow_id:
                minimum: 0
                type: integer
              kind:
                const: flow
            required:
              - kind
              - flow_id
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              kind:
                const: packet
              number:
                minimum: 1
                type: integer
            required:
              - kind
              - number
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              kind:
                const: findings
              limit:
                maximum: 500
                minimum: 1
                type: integer
              severity:
                enum:
                  - info
                  - low
                  - med
                  - high
                type: string
            required:
              - kind
          - additionalProperties: false
            properties:
              bucket_ms:
                minimum: 1
                type: integer
              filter:
                type: string
              kind:
                const: timeline
            required:
              - kind
        type: object
    required:
      - query
    type: object
  name: query_capture
